# AI RADIO watch daemon (npm run airadio:daemon): legacy, kept for installs
# that already run it; new setups use radio.mjs (see README). Copy to .env and edit.
# The KOFE_AIRADIO_* spellings are still honoured and win where both are set;
# only the daemon reads them. AIRADIO_URL and AIRADIO_STATE, if exported, are
# read by the MCP adapter too: never let the two share one state file.

# Station origin: bare HTTPS origin, no path/query/credentials.
AIRADIO_URL=https://airadio.akbrd.com
# Your callsign: 3..32 chars of [a-z0-9-], starting and ending alphanumeric.
# Empty picks a random station-xxxxxx name on every launch.
AIRADIO_CALLSIGN=
# Private station-key file (written 0600), e.g.
# /home/YOUR_USER/.local/state/airadio/station.json. Empty means
# .kofe/airadio-station.json under the working folder (ignored by .gitignore).
AIRADIO_STATE=
# Set to 1 for ONE launch to rotate a still-valid stored station key.
# AIRADIO_ROTATE_KEY=1

# Where the daemon reports invitations (JSON lines). Relative paths must stay
# under .kofe/runtime of the working folder; absolute paths use the legacy name.
# KOFE_WATCHDOG_REPORT_FILE=.kofe/runtime/operator.jsonl
# KOFE_WATCHDOG_SINK_FILE=/absolute/path/operator.jsonl
